        {
          "unit_id": "missing_laptop",
          "title": "The Missing Laptop",
          "description": "Deducciones sobre el pasado y críticas: must have, can't have, might have, should have. Y otros modales en pasado: needn't have, could have, should (expectativa).",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "missing_laptop_lesson",
              "title": "Modals of deduction: past",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "The missing laptop",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "It's gone. My laptop's gone."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "It can't have disappeared. You must have left it somewhere."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "I had it at the conference. I must have put it down when we were talking to Mark."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Or you might have left it in the taxi."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "No, I can't have left it in the taxi. I remember holding it when we got out."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Then someone at the conference must have picked it up by mistake."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Receptionist",
                        "text": "Excuse me, Mr O'Brien? Somebody from the conference centre has just dropped this off for you."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "My laptop! Where did they find it?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Receptionist",
                        "text": "Apparently it was under a chair in the main hall."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "So you must have left it there after all."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "I could have lost the whole demo. Thank goodness for honest people."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "You should have kept it in your bag."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "I know, I know. You don't have to say it."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "That evening, back at the hotel, Daniel can't find his laptop. It has the demo for Mark's project on it."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"You must have left it somewhere.\" This is about…",
                        "options": [
                          "the past",
                          "the present"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"I can't have left it in the taxi.\" Daniel is…",
                        "options": [
                          "sure he didn't",
                          "sure he did"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"You should have kept it in your bag.\" This is…",
                        "options": [
                          "a criticism of a past action",
                          "advice for the future"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "Where was the laptop?",
                        "options": [
                          "under a chair in the main hall",
                          "in the taxi",
                          "in the hotel room"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Modals of deduction: past",
                    "explanation": "Para deducir qué pasó usamos modal + have + participio:\n• must have = seguro que pasó: You must have left it somewhere.\n• can't have = seguro que no pasó: I can't have left it in the taxi.\n• might / may / could have = quizá pasó: You might have left it in the taxi.\n\nOtros usos muy frecuentes:\n• could have = era posible, pero no pasó: I could have lost the whole demo.\n• should have / shouldn't have = crítica o arrepentimiento: You should have kept it in your bag.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Modal",
                        "Significado",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "must have + participio",
                          "seguro que pasó",
                          "You must have left it somewhere."
                        ],
                        [
                          "can't have + participio",
                          "seguro que no pasó",
                          "I can't have left it in the taxi."
                        ],
                        [
                          "might / may have",
                          "quizá pasó",
                          "You might have left it in the taxi."
                        ],
                        [
                          "could have",
                          "era posible (pero no pasó)",
                          "I could have lost the whole demo."
                        ],
                        [
                          "should have",
                          "debería haber… (crítica)",
                          "You should have kept it in your bag."
                        ],
                        [
                          "shouldn't have",
                          "no debería haber…",
                          "I shouldn't have put it down."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "It can't have disappeared. You must have left it somewhere.",
                      "Someone at the conference must have picked it up by mistake.",
                      "I could have lost the whole demo.",
                      "You should have kept it in your bag."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "needn't have, didn't need to, could have",
                    "explanation": "Needn't have + participio: hiciste algo que al final no hacía falta: You needn't have worried. The laptop was safe (te preocupaste, pero no hacía falta).\n\nDidn't need to + verbo: no era necesario, y normalmente no se hizo: We didn't need to call the police, because the receptionist had it.\n\nCould have + participio tiene dos usos más: algo que pudo pasar y no pasó (I could have lost the whole demo) y un reproche (You could have told me! = podrías habérmelo dicho).\n\nShould + verbo también expresa lo que esperamos que pase: The taxi should be here in five minutes. Y en pasado: The parcel should have arrived by now (debería haber llegado ya, y no ha llegado).",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Estructura",
                        "Ejemplo",
                        "Significado"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "needn't have + participio",
                          "You needn't have worried.",
                          "lo hiciste, pero no hacía falta"
                        ],
                        [
                          "didn't need to + verbo",
                          "We didn't need to call the police.",
                          "no hacía falta (y no se hizo)"
                        ],
                        [
                          "could have + participio",
                          "I could have lost the demo.",
                          "pudo pasar, pero no pasó"
                        ],
                        [
                          "could have + participio",
                          "You could have told me!",
                          "reproche"
                        ],
                        [
                          "should have (expectativa)",
                          "Mark should have replied by now.",
                          "lo normal sería que ya…"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "You needn't have run back to the hotel. Someone had already found it.",
                      "We didn't need to buy a new laptop, thank goodness.",
                      "You could have told me you'd lost it!",
                      "Mark's email should have arrived by now. Let me check again."
                    ]
                  }
                },
